[2026-03-14T19:53:54.677Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K8wjc4QwGvzjgwKEFzzNdc","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Google Flights Clone — Test Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Page: Search Page (Home)\n     4→\n     5→### Components\n     6→- TripTypeSelector\n     7→- PassengerCountSelector\n     8→- CabinClassSelector\n     9→- AirportAutocomplete\n    10→- DatePicker\n    11→- SearchButton\n    12→- RecentSearches\n    13→- PopularDestinations\n    14→\n    15→### TripTypeSelector\n    16→\n    17→#### Test: TripTypeSelector displays default \"Round trip\" selection\n    18→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    19→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with default settings\n    20→- **Action**: User observes the trip type selector\n    21→- **Expected**: The selector displays \"Round trip\" as the default selected option. It is rendered as a custom dropdown (not a native select element).\n    22→\n    23→#### Test: TripTypeSelector opens dropdown and shows all options\n    24→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    25→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, trip type selector is closed\n    26→- **Action**: User clicks the trip type selector\n    27→- **Expected**: A dropdown menu opens showing three options: \"Round trip\", \"One way\", and \"Multi-city\". Each option is clickable.\n    28→\n    29→#### Test: TripTypeSelector selects \"One way\" and hides return date\n    30→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector, DatePicker\n    31→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded with \"Round trip\" selected, return date picker is visible\n    32→- **Action**: User clicks the trip type selector and selects \"One way\"\n    33→- **Expected**: The selector updates to show \"One way\". The return date picker is hidden. The dropdown closes.\n    34→\n    35→#### Test: TripTypeSelector selects \"Multi-city\" option\n    36→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    37→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded with \"Round trip\" selected\n    38→- **Action**: User clicks the trip type selector and selects \"Multi-city\"\n    39→- **Expected**: The selector updates to show \"Multi-city\". The search form adjusts to support multi-city input (multiple origin/destination pairs).\n    40→\n    41→#### Test: TripTypeSelector switches back to \"Round trip\" from \"One way\"\n    42→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector, DatePicker\n    43→- **Initial state**: \"One way\" is currently selected, return date picker is hidden\n    44→- **Action**: User clicks the trip type selector and selects \"Round trip\"\n    45→- **Expected**: The selector updates to show \"Round trip\". The return date picker becomes visible again.\n    46→\n    47→#### Test: TripTypeSelector closes dropdown when clicking outside\n    48→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    49→- **Initial state**: Trip type dropdown is open\n    50→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown\n    51→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes without changing the selection.\n    52→\n    53→#### Test: TripTypeSelector can be used multiple times in sequence\n    54→- **Components**: TripTypeSelector\n    55→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded with default \"Round trip\"\n    56→- **Action**: User selects \"One way\", then interacts with another element (e.g., clicks airport field), then opens the trip type selector again and selects \"Round trip\"\n    57→- **Expected**: Each interaction correctly updates the selector. The dropdown opens and closes properly on each use. The final state shows \"Round trip\" selected.\n    58→\n    59→### PassengerCountSelector\n    60→\n    61→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector displays default \"1 Adult\"\n    62→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    63→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with default settings\n    64→- **Action**: User observes the passenger count selector\n    65→- **Expected**: The selector displays \"1\" or \"1 Adult\" as the default.\n    66→\n    67→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector opens dropdown with passenger categories\n    68→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    69→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, passenger selector is closed\n    70→- **Action**: User clicks the passenger count selector\n    71→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing three categories: Adults, Children, and Infants. Each category has a label, a current count, and \"+\" and \"−\" buttons.\n    72→\n    73→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments adult count\n    74→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    75→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults count is 1\n    76→- **Action**: User clicks the \"+\" button next to Adults\n    77→- **Expected**: Adults count increases to 2. The selector label updates to reflect the new total (e.g., \"2 passengers\" or \"2 Adults\").\n    78→\n    79→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector decrements adult count with minimum of 1\n    80→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    81→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults count is 1\n    82→- **Action**: User clicks the \"−\" button next to Adults\n    83→- **Expected**: Adults count remains at 1. The \"−\" button is disabled or has no effect since at least 1 adult is required.\n    84→\n    85→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments and decrements children\n    86→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    87→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Children count is 0\n    88→- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Children twice, then clicks \"−\" once\n    89→- **Expected**: Children count goes to 1. The total passenger display updates accordingly.\n    90→\n    91→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector increments and decrements infants\n    92→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    93→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Infants count is 0\n    94→- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Infants\n    95→- **Expected**: Infants count increases to 1. The total passenger display updates accordingly.\n    96→\n    97→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector prevents infants exceeding adults\n    98→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n    99→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults = 1, Infants = 1\n   100→- **Action**: User clicks \"+\" next to Infants\n   101→- **Expected**: Infants count remains at 1 (cannot exceed number of adults). The \"+\" button is disabled or has no effect.\n   102→\n   103→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector closes dropdown and retains values\n   104→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n   105→- **Initial state**: Passenger dropdown is open, Adults = 2, Children = 1, Infants = 0\n   106→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown to close it\n   107→- **Expected**: Dropdown closes. The selector label shows the updated total (e.g., \"3 passengers\"). Reopening the dropdown shows the same values (2 Adults, 1 Child, 0 Infants).\n   108→\n   109→#### Test: PassengerCountSelector can be used repeatedly\n   110→- **Components**: PassengerCountSelector\n   111→- **Initial state**: Search page with default passenger counts\n   112→- **Action**: User opens the selector, adds 1 adult, closes it, interacts with another element (e.g., selects cabin class), then reopens the passenger selector and adds 1 child\n   113→- **Expected**: All values persist correctly between opens. Final state shows 2 Adults, 1 Child. The selector works correctly on each subsequent use.\n   114→\n   115→### CabinClassSelector\n   116→\n   117→#### Test: CabinClassSelector displays default \"Economy\"\n   118→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   119→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with default settings\n   120→- **Action**: User observes the cabin class selector\n   121→- **Expected**: The selector displays \"Economy\" as the default selected cabin class. It is rendered as a custom dropdown.\n   122→\n   123→#### Test: CabinClassSelector opens dropdown showing all cabin classes\n   124→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   125→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, cabin class selector is closed\n   126→- **Action**: User clicks the cabin class selector\n   127→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing four options: \"Economy\", \"Premium Economy\", \"Business\", and \"First\".\n   128→\n   129→#### Test: CabinClassSelector selects \"Business\" class\n   130→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   131→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open with \"Economy\" selected\n   132→- **Action**: User clicks \"Business\"\n   133→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The selector label updates to \"Business\".\n   134→\n   135→#### Test: CabinClassSelector selects \"Premium Economy\" class\n   136→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   137→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open\n   138→- **Action**: User clicks \"Premium Economy\"\n   139→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The selector label updates to \"Premium Economy\".\n   140→\n   141→#### Test: CabinClassSelector selects \"First\" class\n   142→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   143→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open\n   144→- **Action**: User clicks \"First\"\n   145→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. The selector label updates to \"First\".\n   146→\n   147→#### Test: CabinClassSelector closes dropdown when clicking outside\n   148→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   149→- **Initial state**: Cabin class dropdown is open\n   150→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown\n   151→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes without changing the selection.\n   152→\n   153→#### Test: CabinClassSelector can be changed multiple times\n   154→- **Components**: CabinClassSelector\n   155→- **Initial state**: Search page with \"Economy\" selected\n   156→- **Action**: User selects \"Business\", interacts with another element, then reopens and selects \"First\", then reopens and selects \"Economy\"\n   157→- **Expected**: Each selection correctly updates the label. The final state shows \"Economy\". The dropdown works correctly on each use.\n   158→\n   159→### AirportAutocomplete\n   160→\n   161→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete origin field shows placeholder text\n   162→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   163→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with empty origin field\n   164→- **Action**: User observes the origin airport field\n   165→- **Expected**: The field displays placeholder text indicating the user should enter an origin (e.g., \"Where from?\").\n   166→\n   167→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete destination field shows placeholder text\n   168→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   169→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with empty destination field\n   170→- **Action**: User observes the destination airport field\n   171→- **Expected**: The field displays placeholder text indicating the user should enter a destination (e.g., \"Where to?\").\n   172→\n   173→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete shows suggestions when typing airport name\n   174→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   175→- **Initial state**: Origin field is focused and empty\n   176→- **Action**: User types \"Los Angeles\" into the origin field\n   177→- **Expected**: A suggestion dropdown appears showing matching airports, including \"Los Angeles International Airport (LAX)\". Each suggestion shows the airport name and IATA code.\n   178→\n   179→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete shows suggestions when typing IATA code\n   180→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   181→- **Initial state**: Origin field is focused and empty\n   182→- **Action**: User types \"JFK\" into the origin field\n   183→- **Expected**: A suggestion dropdown appears showing \"John F. Kennedy International Airport (JFK)\" as a match.\n   184→\n   185→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete shows suggestions when typing city name\n   186→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   187→- **Initial state**: Destination field is focused and empty\n   188→- **Action**: User types \"London\" into the destination field\n   189→- **Expected**: A suggestion dropdown appears showing London-area airports (e.g., \"London Heathrow (LHR)\").\n   190→\n   191→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete selects a suggestion and populates the field\n   192→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   193→- **Initial state**: User has typed \"Los\" in the origin field, suggestions are visible\n   194→- **Action**: User clicks on \"Los Angeles International Airport (LAX)\" from the suggestions\n   195→- **Expected**: The origin field is populated with the selected airport (showing name and/or code). The suggestion dropdown closes.\n   196→\n   197→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete swap button exchanges origin and destination\n   198→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   199→- **Initial state**: Origin is set to \"LAX\" and destination is set to \"JFK\"\n   200→- **Action**: User clicks the swap button between origin and destination fields\n   201→- **Expected**: Origin becomes \"JFK\" and destination becomes \"LAX\". Both fields update their displayed values.\n   202→\n   203→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete swap button works with empty fields\n   204→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   205→- **Initial state**: Origin is set to \"LAX\", destination is empty\n   206→- **Action**: User clicks the swap button\n   207→- **Expected**: Origin becomes empty, destination becomes \"LAX\".\n   208→\n   209→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete clears field and shows new suggestions\n   210→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   211→- **Initial state**: Origin field has \"LAX\" selected\n   212→- **Action**: User clears the origin field and types \"San\"\n   213→- **Expected**: The field clears the previous selection. New suggestions appear for airports matching \"San\" (e.g., \"San Francisco International Airport (SFO)\", \"San Diego International Airport (SAN)\").\n   214→\n   215→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete shows no results for invalid query\n   216→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   217→- **Initial state**: Origin field is focused\n   218→- **Action**: User types \"xyznonexistent\" into the origin field\n   219→- **Expected**: The suggestion dropdown shows a \"No airports found\" message or similar empty state.\n   220→\n   221→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete destination works after using origin\n   222→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   223→- **Initial state**: Origin is set to \"LAX\"\n   224→- **Action**: User clicks the destination field and types \"New York\"\n   225→- **Expected**: Suggestions appear for New York area airports. Selecting one populates the destination. Both origin and destination retain their values.\n   226→\n   227→#### Test: AirportAutocomplete can be used repeatedly\n   228→- **Components**: AirportAutocomplete\n   229→- **Initial state**: Origin and destination are both populated\n   230→- **Action**: User clears origin, types a new airport, selects it, then clears destination, types a new airport, and selects it\n   231→- **Expected**: Both fields update correctly. Autocomplete suggestions work properly on each subsequent use.\n   232→\n   233→### DatePicker\n   234→\n   235→#### Test: DatePicker departure field shows placeholder\n   236→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   237→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with no date selected\n   238→- **Action**: User observes the departure date picker\n   239→- **Expected**: The departure date field shows a placeholder (e.g., \"Departure\" or a date format hint).\n   240→\n   241→#### Test: DatePicker return field shows placeholder when Round trip\n   242→- **Components**: DatePicker, TripTypeSelector\n   243→- **Initial state**: Search page loads with \"Round trip\" selected\n   244→- **Action**: User observes the return date picker\n   245→- **Expected**: The return date field is visible and shows a placeholder (e.g., \"Return\" or a date format hint).\n   246→\n   247→#### Test: DatePicker opens calendar on departure field click\n   248→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   249→- **Initial state**: Search page loaded, departure date field is not focused\n   250→- **Action**: User clicks the departure date field\n   251→- **Expected**: A calendar popup opens showing the current month. Past dates are disabled/grayed out. Users can navigate between months.\n   252→\n   253→#### Test: DatePicker selects a departure date\n   254→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   255→- **Initial state**: Departure date calendar is open\n   256→- **Action**: User clicks a future date (e.g., March 25)\n   257→- **Expected**: The date is selected and displayed in the departure field (e.g., \"Mar 25\" or \"2026-03-25\"). The calendar closes or shifts focus to the return date.\n   258→\n   259→#### Test: DatePicker selects a return date after departure\n   260→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   261→- **Initial state**: Departure date is set to March 25, return date calendar is open\n   262→- **Action**: User clicks a date after the departure date (e.g., April 1)\n   263→- **Expected**: The return date is set and displayed. Dates before the departure date are disabled in the return calendar.\n   264→\n   265→#### Test: DatePicker prevents selecting return date before departure\n   266→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   267→- **Initial state**: Departure date is set to March 25, return date calendar is open\n   268→- **Action**: User attempts to click March 20 (before departure)\n   269→- **Expected**: The date cannot be selected. It appears disabled/grayed out.\n   270→\n   271→#### Test: DatePicker navigates to next month\n   272→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   273→- **Initial state**: Calendar is open showing the current month\n   274→- **Action**: User clicks the \"next month\" arrow button\n   275→- **Expected**: The calendar displays the next month's dates.\n   276→\n   277→#### Test: DatePicker navigates to previous month (not before current)\n   278→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   279→- **Initial state**: Calendar is open showing the current month\n   280→- **Action**: User clicks the \"previous month\" arrow button\n   281→- **Expected**: If current month is shown, the previous button is disabled or has no effect (cannot navigate to past months). If a future month is shown, it navigates back.\n   282→\n   283→#### Test: DatePicker return field hidden when One way selected\n   284→- **Components**: DatePicker, TripTypeSelector\n   285→- **Initial state**: \"One way\" trip type is selected\n   286→- **Action**: User observes the date picker area\n   287→- **Expected**: Only the departure date picker is visible. The return date picker is not rendered.\n   288→\n   289→#### Test: DatePicker retains departure date when switching trip types\n   290→- **Components**: DatePicker, TripTypeSelector\n   291→- **Initial state**: \"Round trip\" selected with departure date March 25 and return date April 1\n   292→- **Action**: User switches to \"One way\" then back to \"Round trip\"\n   293→- **Expected**: The departure date (March 25) is retained. The return date may be cleared or retained depending on implementation.\n   294→\n   295→#### Test: DatePicker can be used repeatedly\n   296→- **Components**: DatePicker\n   297→- **Initial state**: Departure date is set to March 25\n   298→- **Action**: User clicks the departure date field again and selects a different date (e.g., March 28)\n   299→- **Expected**: The departure date updates to March 28. The calendar opens and closes correctly on subsequent uses.\n   300→\n   301→### SearchButton\n   302→\n   303→#### Test: SearchButton is displayed with prominent styling\n   304→- **Components**: SearchButton\n   305→- **Initial state**: Search page is loaded\n   306→- **Action**: User observes the search button\n   307→- **Expected**: A prominent search button is visible with the primary blue color (#1A73E8) and clear text (e.g., \"Search\" or a search icon). The button has a hover effect.\n   308→\n   309→#### Test: SearchButton navigates to results page with valid inputs\n   310→- **Components**: SearchButton, AirportAutocomplete, DatePicker\n   311→- **Initial state**: Origin is \"LAX\", destination is \"JFK\", departure date is March 25, return date is April 1, trip type is \"Round trip\"\n   312→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   313→- **Expected**: The app navigates to the Search Results page. The search parameters are passed to the results page. A recent search entry is saved to the database.\n   314→\n   315→#### Test: SearchButton shows validation error when origin is missing\n   316→- **Components**: SearchButton, AirportAutocomplete\n   317→- **Initial state**: Origin is empty, destination is \"JFK\", dates are set\n   318→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   319→- **Expected**: The search is not executed. A validation error is shown near the origin field indicating it is required.\n   320→\n   321→#### Test: SearchButton shows validation error when destination is missing\n   322→- **Components**: SearchButton, AirportAutocomplete\n   323→- **Initial state**: Origin is \"LAX\", destination is empty, dates are set\n   324→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   325→- **Expected**: The search is not executed. A validation error is shown near the destination field indicating it is required.\n   326→\n   327→#### Test: SearchButton shows validation error when departure date is missing\n   328→- **Components**: SearchButton, DatePicker\n   329→- **Initial state**: Origin and destination are set, departure date is empty\n   330→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   331→- **Expected**: The search is not executed. A validation error is shown near the departure date field.\n   332→\n   333→#### Test: SearchButton shows validation error when return date is missing for round trip\n   334→- **Components**: SearchButton, DatePicker, TripTypeSelector\n   335→- **Initial state**: \"Round trip\" selected, origin and destination set, departure date set, return date empty\n   336→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   337→- **Expected**: The search is not executed. A validation error is shown near the return date field.\n   338→\n   339→#### Test: SearchButton works for One way trip without return date\n   340→- **Components**: SearchButton, TripTypeSelector\n   341→- **Initial state**: \"One way\" selected, origin is \"LAX\", destination is \"JFK\", departure date is set\n   342→- **Action**: User clicks the Search button\n   343→- **Expected**: The search executes successfully and navigates to the results page. No validation error for missing return date.\n   344→\n   345→#### Test: SearchButton saves search to recent searches\n   346→- **Components**: SearchButton, RecentSearches\n   347→- **Initial state**: Valid search parameters filled in, no recent searches\n   348→- **Action**: User clicks Search, then navigates back to the Search page\n   349→- **Expected**: The search appears in the recent searches section showing origin → destination, dates, and passenger count.\n   350→\n   351→### RecentSearches\n   352→\n   353→#### Test: RecentSearches shows empty state when no searches exist\n   354→- **Components**: RecentSearches\n   355→- **Initial state**: New session with no previous searches\n   356→- **Action**: User observes the area below the search form\n   357→- **Expected**: The recent searches section is either hidden or displays an empty state message (e.g., \"No recent searches\").\n   358→\n   359→#### Test: RecentSearches displays a recent search entry\n   360→- **Components**: RecentSearches\n   361→- **Initial state**: User has performed one search (LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, 1 adult)\n   362→- **Action**: User navigates back to the search page and observes recent searches\n   363→- **Expected**: One recent search entry is displayed showing \"LAX → JFK\", the dates \"Mar 25 – Apr 1\", and \"1 passenger\".\n   364→\n   365→#### Test: RecentSearches clicking a recent search re-populates the form\n   366→- **Components**: RecentSearches, AirportAutocomplete, DatePicker, PassengerCountSelector, TripTypeSelector, CabinClassSelector\n   367→- **Initial state**: A recent search exists (LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, 2 adults, Business class, Round trip)\n   368→- **Action**: User clicks on the recent search entry\n   369→- **Expected**: The search form is populated with the recent search parameters: origin = LAX, destination = JFK, departure = Mar 25, return = Apr 1, passengers = 2 adults, cabin class = Business, trip type = Round trip. The search is executed and the app navigates to the results page.\n   370→\n   371→#### Test: RecentSearches displays multiple recent searches in order\n   372→- **Components**: RecentSearches\n   373→- **Initial state**: User has performed 3 searches in order: (1) LAX→JFK, (2) SFO→ORD, (3) LAX→LHR\n   374→- **Action**: User navigates back to the search page\n   375→- **Expected**: All three recent searches are displayed with the most recent (LAX→LHR) shown first.\n   376→\n   377→#### Test: RecentSearches updates after a new search\n   378→- **Components**: RecentSearches, SearchButton\n   379→- **Initial state**: One recent search exists (LAX → JFK)\n   380→- **Action**: User performs a new search (SFO → ORD) and returns to the search page\n   381→- **Expected**: Two recent searches are displayed. The new search (SFO → ORD) appears first, followed by the older one (LAX → JFK).\n   382→\n   383→### PopularDestinations\n   384→\n   385→#### Test: PopularDestinations grid is displayed on search page\n   386→- **Components**: PopularDestinations\n   387→- **Initial state**: Search page loads\n   388→- **Action**: User scrolls to see the popular destinations section below the search form\n   389→- **Expected**: A grid of destination cards is visible. Each card shows a city name, country, a colored gradient placeholder image, and a \"from $X\" starting price.\n   390→\n   391→#### Test: PopularDestinations card shows city, country, and price\n   392→- **Components**: PopularDestinations\n   393→- **Initial state**: Popular destinations section is visible\n   394→- **Action**: User examines a destination card\n   395→- **Expected**: The card displays the destination city name, country name, a colored gradient image placeholder, and a starting price (e.g., \"from $199\").\n   396→\n   397→#### Test: PopularDestinations clicking a card initiates a search\n   398→- **Components**: PopularDestinations, AirportAutocomplete, SearchButton\n   399→- **Initial state**: Popular destinations section is visible, user has no origin set\n   400→- **Action**: User clicks on a destination card (e.g., \"Tokyo, Japan\")\n   401→- **Expected**: The destination field is populated with the corresponding airport. A search is initiated to that destination (the origin may use a default or prompt the user to enter one).\n   402→\n   403→#### Test: PopularDestinations displays multiple cards in grid layout\n   404→- **Components**: PopularDestinations\n   405→- **Initial state**: Search page loads\n   406→- **Action**: User observes the popular destinations section\n   407→- **Expected**: Multiple destination cards are displayed in a responsive grid layout (e.g., 3-4 cards per row on desktop).\n   408→\n   409→#### Test: PopularDestinations cards have hover effect\n   410→- **Components**: PopularDestinations\n   411→- **Initial state**: Popular destinations section is visible\n   412→- **Action**: User hovers over a destination card\n   413→- **Expected**: The card shows a visual hover effect (e.g., shadow increase, slight scale, or color change) indicating it is interactive/clickable.\n   414→\n   415→## Page: Search Results\n   416→\n   417→### Components\n   418→- SearchSummaryBar\n   419→- FilterSidebar\n   420→- FlightResultCard\n   421→- TrackPricesToggle\n   422→- Pagination\n   423→\n   424→### SearchSummaryBar\n   425→\n   426→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar displays search parameters after search\n   427→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar\n   428→- **Initial state**: User searched LAX → JFK, Mar 25 – Apr 1, 1 adult, Economy, Round trip\n   429→- **Action**: User observes the summary bar at the top of the results page\n   430→- **Expected**: The bar displays origin \"LAX\", destination \"JFK\", dates \"Mar 25 – Apr 1\", \"1 adult\", and \"Economy\" inline. Each parameter is visually distinct and clickable.\n   431→\n   432→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit origin airport\n   433→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, AirportAutocomplete\n   434→- **Initial state**: Results page showing LAX → JFK search\n   435→- **Action**: User clicks the origin parameter (\"LAX\") in the summary bar\n   436→- **Expected**: An inline editor opens with an airport autocomplete field pre-filled with \"LAX\". User types \"SFO\", selects \"San Francisco International Airport (SFO)\" from suggestions, and confirms. The search re-executes with SFO → JFK and results update.\n   437→\n   438→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit destination airport\n   439→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, AirportAutocomplete\n   440→- **Initial state**: Results page showing LAX → JFK search\n   441→- **Action**: User clicks the destination parameter (\"JFK\") in the summary bar\n   442→- **Expected**: An inline editor opens with an airport autocomplete field pre-filled with \"JFK\". User types \"ORD\", selects \"O'Hare International Airport (ORD)\" from suggestions, and confirms. The search re-executes with LAX → ORD and results update.\n   443→\n   444→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit departure date\n   445→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, DatePicker\n   446→- **Initial state**: Results page showing search with departure Mar 25\n   447→- **Action**: User clicks the departure date parameter in the summary bar\n   448→- **Expected**: A date picker opens with Mar 25 selected. User selects Mar 28. The search re-executes with the new departure date and results update.\n   449→\n   450→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit return date\n   451→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, DatePicker\n   452→- **Initial state**: Results page showing round trip search with return Apr 1\n   453→- **Action**: User clicks the return date parameter in the summary bar\n   454→- **Expected**: A date picker opens with Apr 1 selected. User selects Apr 5. The search re-executes with the new return date and results update.\n   455→\n   456→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit passengers\n   457→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, PassengerCountSelector\n   458→- **Initial state**: Results page showing search with 1 adult\n   459→- **Action**: User clicks the passenger count parameter in the summary bar\n   460→- **Expected**: A passenger selector dropdown opens showing Adults: 1, Children: 0, Infants: 0. User increments adults to 2 and closes. The search re-executes with 2 adults and results update with new pricing.\n   461→\n   462→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline edit cabin class\n   463→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar, CabinClassSelector\n   464→- **Initial state**: Results page showing Economy search\n   465→- **Action**: User clicks the cabin class parameter in the summary bar\n   466→- **Expected**: A dropdown opens showing Economy, Premium Economy, Business, First. User selects \"Business\". The search re-executes with Business class and results update with new pricing.\n   467→\n   468→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar inline editor closes without changes on outside click\n   469→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar\n   470→- **Initial state**: User has clicked the origin parameter and the inline editor is open\n   471→- **Action**: User clicks outside the inline editor\n   472→- **Expected**: The inline editor closes. The original search parameters are unchanged. No re-search occurs.\n   473→\n   474→#### Test: SearchSummaryBar can be edited multiple times in sequence\n   475→- **Components**: SearchSummaryBar\n   476→- **Initial state**: Results page showing LAX → JFK search\n   477→- **Action**: User edits origin to SFO (results update), then edits cabin class to Business (results update again)\n   478→- **Expected**: Each edit triggers a new search. The summary bar reflects all changes: SFO → JFK, Business. Results correspond to the updated parameters.\n   479→\n   480→### FilterSidebar\n   481→\n   482→#### Test: FilterSidebar displays all filter sections\n   483→- **Components**: FilterSidebar\n   484→- **Initial state**: Search results page loaded with results\n   485→- **Action**: User observes the left sidebar\n   486→- **Expected**: The sidebar displays filter sections: Stops, Airlines, Price range, Duration range, Departure time, and a Sort by dropdown. All sections are visible and labeled.\n   487→\n   488→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check Nonstop\n   489→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   490→- **Initial state**: Results page with mix of nonstop and connecting flights\n   491→- **Action**: User checks the \"Nonstop\" checkbox in the Stops filter\n   492→- **Expected**: Only nonstop flights are displayed in the results list. Flights with 1+ stops are hidden.\n   493→\n   494→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check 1 stop\n   495→- **Components**: FilterSidebar, FlightResultCard\n   496→- **Initial state**: Results page with mix of nonstop and connecting flights, no filters applied\n   497→- **Action**: User checks the \"1 stop\" checkbox\n   498→- **Expected**: Only 1-stop flights are displayed. Nonstop and 2+ stop flights are hidden.\n   499→\n   500→#### Test: FilterSidebar stops filter — check multiple options"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WHJyBsfTCpeu9AQnDHA24R","session_id":"755439b7-7306-4724-ae36-7d6e61e30f0f","uuid":"b6882ee6-1ead-434a-b2bd-4fd320f0559d"}
